---
layout: base.njk
title: Arfat Salman · Full-stack software engineer in Oslo
---

<section class="hero row" aria-labelledby="name">
  <figure class="portrait">
    <img src="/assets/profile.jpeg" width="450" height="450" fetchpriority="high" alt="Portrait of Arfat Salman in glasses and a checked shirt." />
    <figcaption><span class="fig">Fig. 1</span> The author, probably about to explain closures.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="hero-body">
    <p class="kicker">{{ site.role }} · {{ site.location }}</p>
    <h1 id="name">Arfat <em>Salman</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I design and build software end to end, from the interface down to the systems
      <span class="pen">underneath<svg viewBox="0 0 100 10" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 6.5 C 18 3, 34 8.5, 52 5.5 S 84 3.5, 99 6" /></svg></span>,
      and I like explaining how it all works.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full-stack engineer and instructor<sup class="ref" aria-hidden="true"></sup>. Equally at home in a React
      component, an API or an architecture diagram, and most interested in software that keeps working as it
      grows. These days I’m in Oslo.
    </p>
    <p class="jump">
      <a href="#stack">Across the stack</a>
      <a href="#work">Selected work</a>
      <a href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <aside class="note">
    Hence the syllabus in § 03: everything I’ve written, arranged the way I’d teach it.
  </aside>
</section>

<section class="section" id="stack" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
  <header class="section-head row">
    <p class="label">§ 01</p>
    <h2 id="stack-title">Across the stack</h2>
  </header>

  <div class="row">
    <div></div>
    <figure class="layers-fig">
      <ol class="layers">
        {% for layer in practice %}
        <li class="layer">
          <h3 class="layer-name">
            <span class="meta">{{ layer.area }}</span>
            <span class="title">{{ layer.title }}</span>
          </h3>
          <div class="layer-body">
            <p>{{ layer.body }}</p>
            <ul class="stack" aria-label="Tools">
              {% for tag in layer.tags %}<li>{{ tag }}</li>{% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="fig">Fig. 2</span> Where I work: all the way down<sup class="ref" aria-hidden="true"></sup>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <aside class="note">
      My writing in § 03 is mostly JavaScript; that’s what I taught. The work itself goes further down.
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <header class="section-head row">
    <p class="label">§ 02</p>
    <h2 id="work-title">Selected work</h2>
  </header>

  {% for project in projects %}
  <article class="item row">
    <div class="item-index">
      <span class="num">{{ loop.index | pad }}</span>
      <span class="meta">{{ project.kind }} · {{ project.year }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="item-body">
      <h3>{{ project.title }}</h3>
      <p class="summary">{{ project.summary }}{% if project.note %}<sup class="ref" aria-hidden="true"></sup>{% endif %}</p>
      <p>{{ project.body | safe }}</p>
      <ul class="stack" aria-label="Built with">
        {% for tech in project.stack %}<li>{{ tech }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <p class="links">
        {% for link in project.links %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endfor %}
      </p>
    </div>
    {% if project.note %}<aside class="note">{{ project.note | safe }}</aside>{% endif %}
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section class="section" id="syllabus" aria-labelledby="syllabus-title">
  <header class="section-head row">
    <p class="label">§ 03</p>
    <h2 id="syllabus-title">A short syllabus</h2>
  </header>

  <div class="row intro">
    <div></div>
    <div>
      <p>
        I’ve worked as an instructor as well as a developer, and I still think the best way to learn a thing
        is to explain it to someone. Here is my writing arranged as a short course on JavaScript.
        Every reading is something I wrote<sup class="ref" aria-hidden="true"></sup>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="note">
      {{ syllabus.articleCount }} articles, published in <em>Bits and Pieces</em> and <em>codeburst</em> for
      2.5K followers on <a href="https://medium.com/@arfatsalman">Medium</a>.
    </aside>
  </div>

  <ol class="units">
    {% for unit in syllabus.units %}
    <li class="unit row">
      <p class="item-index">
        <span class="meta">Unit</span>
        <span class="num">{{ loop.index | pad }}</span>
      </p>
      <div class="item-body">
        <h3>{{ unit.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ unit.topics | safe }}</p>
        <ul class="readings" aria-label="Readings">
          {% for r in unit.readings %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.title }}</a>
            <span class="meta">{{ r.where }}{% if r.date %} · {{ r.date | monthYear }}{% endif %}{% if r.minutes %} · {{ r.minutes }} min{% endif %}</span>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <div class="row more">
    <p class="label">Also</p>
    <div>
      <h3>Shorter pieces on Medium</h3>
      <ul class="readings">
        {% for r in syllabus.more %}
        <li>
          <a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.title }}</a>
          <span class="meta">{{ r.where }} · {{ r.date | monthYear }} · {{ r.minutes }} min</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <header class="section-head row">
    <p class="label">§ 04</p>
    <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
  </header>

  <div class="row">
    <div></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I’m Arfat. I live in Oslo, which I came to for a Master’s in Computer Science at the University of
        Oslo. Before that I worked as a full-stack developer and an instructor: building products across the
        front end and the back end, and teaching other people to do the same.
      </p>
      <p>
        At work I gravitate towards architecture: where the boundaries go, how data moves through a system,
        and what will still hold up when the traffic, the codebase and the team are ten times bigger.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of it, I like programming languages and the tools around them: interpreters, paradigms, and the testing that
        keeps them honest. That curiosity has taken me from Lox to OCaml and Standard ML, and as far as
        testing the SDKs people use to write quantum programs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="note facts" aria-label="Quick facts">
      <dl>
        <dt>Based in</dt>
        <dd>{{ site.location }}</dd>
        <dt>Front end</dt>
        <dd>JavaScript, React</dd>
        <dt>Back end</dt>
        <dd>Node.js, Python</dd>
        <dt>Drawn to</dt>
        <dd>Architecture, languages</dd>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
  <header class="section-head row">
    <p class="label">§ 05</p>
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
  </header>

  <div class="row">
    <div></div>
    <div>
      <p class="big">The quickest way to reach me is email.</p>
      <p class="email" data-email="{{ site.emailEncoded }}">
        <button class="reveal" type="button" hidden>Show my email address</button>
        <a class="email-address" hidden></a>
        <button class="copy" type="button" hidden>Copy</button>
        <span class="copy-status" role="status"></span>
      </p>
      <noscript>
        <p class="email-fallback">
          My email address needs JavaScript to appear. You can also reach me on
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/arfatsalman/">LinkedIn</a>.
        </p>
      </noscript>
      <ul class="elsewhere" aria-label="Elsewhere">
        {% for link in site.links %}
        <li><a href="{{ link.url }}"><span class="site">{{ link.label }}</span> <span class="handle">{{ link.handle }}</span></a></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
